                  { elem: "OaML", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outlineAndFill },
                  { elem: "OLNb", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outlineAndFill },
                  { elem: "OaHb", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outlineAndFill },
                  { elem: "Hf", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] } },
            { text: "But parallelepipedal solids on equal bases and of the same height equal one another,",
              visible: LH,
              highlighted: ["pMN","pDF"] },
            { text: "therefore the solid {HL|sLH} equals the solid {EK|sEK}.",
              visible: LH,
              highlighted: ["sLH","sEK"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "solid HL = solid EK", ref: "XI.31" }] },
            { text: "And {LH|sLH} is the solid formed out of {A}, {B}, and {C}, and {EK|sEK} is the solid on {B},",
              visible: LH,
              highlighted: ["sLH","sEK"] },
            { text: "therefore the parallelepipedal solid formed out of {A}, {B}, and {C} equals the solid on {B}",
              visible: LH,
              highlighted: ["sLH","sEK"] },
            { text: "which is equilateral, but equiangular with the aforesaid solid.",
              visible: LH,
              highlighted: ["sEK"] },
            { text: "Therefore, if three straight lines are proportional,",
              visible: LH,
              highlighted: ["A","B","C"] },
            { text: "then the parallelepipedal solid formed out of the three equals the parallelepipedal solid on the mean",
              visible: LH,
              highlighted: ["sLH","sEK"] },
            { text: "which is equilateral, but equiangular with the aforesaid solid.",
              visible: LH,
              highlighted: ["sEK","sLH"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "Q.E.D." }] }
        ],
        resolveJustification: function(ref) {
            if (ref === "XI.36") return "#prop";
            return (window.eucrefs && window.eucrefs[ref]) || null;
        }
    });

    // Per-page citation lookup for the slideshow's resolveJustification.
    window.eucrefs = (window.eucrefs || {});
    Object.assign(window.eucrefs, {
        "I.3":       "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI3/",
        "VI.4":      "/elements/books/bookVI/propositions/propVI4/",
        "XI.31":     "/elements/books/bookXI/propositions/propXI31/",
        "XI.35.Cor": "/elements/books/bookXI/propositions/propXI35/#cor"
    });
</script>
</figure>

Set out the solid angle at {E} contained by the angles {DEG|angDEG}, {GEF|angGEF}, and {FED|angFED}, and make each of the straight lines {DE|ED}, {GE|EG}, and {EF} equal to {B}. Complete the parallelepipedal solid {EK|sEK}. Make {LM} equal to {A}. Construct a solid angle at the point {L} on the straight line {LM} equal to the solid angle at {E}, namely that contained by {NLO|angNLO}, {OLM|angOLM}, and {MLN|angMLN}. Make {LO} equal to {B}, and {LN} equal to {C}. [!just I.3]

Now, since {A} is to {B} as {B} is to {C}, while {A} equals {LM}, and {B} equals each of the straight lines {LO}, {ED}, and {C} to {LN}, therefore {LM} is to {EF} as {DE|ED} is to {LN}. Thus the sides about the equal angles {NLM|angMLN}, {DEF|angFED} are reciprocally proportional, therefore the parallelogram {MN|pMN} equals the parallelogram {DF|pDF}. [!just VI.4]

And, since the angles {DEF|angFED} and {NLM|angMLN} are two plane rectilinear angles, and on them the elevated straight lines {LO} and {EG} are set up which equal one an other and contain equal angles with the original straight lines respectively, therefore the perpendiculars drawn from the points {G} and {O} to the planes through {NL|LN} and {LM} and through {DE|ED} and {EF} equal one another, therefore the solids {LH|sLH} and {EK|sEK} are of the same height. [!just XI.35.Cor]

But parallelepipedal solids on equal bases and of the same height equal one another, therefore the solid {HL|sLH} equals the solid {EK|sEK}. [!just XI.31]

And {LH|sLH} is the solid formed out of {A}, {B}, and {C}, and {EK|sEK} is the solid on {B}, therefore the parallelepipedal solid formed out of {A}, {B}, and {C} equals the solid on *B* which is equilateral, but equiangular with the aforesaid solid.

Therefore, *if three straight lines are proportional, then the parallelepipedal solid formed out of the three equals the parallelepipedal solid on the mean which is equilateral, but equiangular with the aforesaid solid.*

<div class="qed">Q.E.D.</div>
----
guide: This straightforward proof depends on viewing the two parallelepipeds as having the same height, which they do if the base of the first is taken to be the parallelogram {MN|pMN} and the base of the second the parallelogram {DF|pDF}.
